    skos:definition "The bark of the _Mimosa decurrens_, which abounds in Australia and Van Diemen's Land, is found to be a very powerful tanning agent. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854, Project Gutenberg #15191)]"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "doc_mimosa_bark" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mimosa Bark"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0041 (Bark For Tanners and Dyers Use). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854, Project Gutenberg #15191)."@en ;
